==English==

===Etymology===
From {{affix|en|phyto-|-tomy}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|botany|dated}} The study of the internal structures of {{l|en|plant|plants}}.
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Elements of the Philosophy of Plants|author=Augustin Pyramus de Candolle; K. Sprengel|origlang=de|tlr=anonymous|year=1821|passage='''Phytotomy''', or anatomy of plants|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=rkwaAAAAYAAJ&dq=%22phytotomy%22&pg=PA173#v=onepage&q=%22phytotomy%22&f=false}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=The Monthly Microscopical Journal|editor=Henry Lawson|year=1877|passage=Having often been asked for the names of the plants in which these crystals may be most conveniently examined and distinguished, probably a short list of them, with a few explanatory remarks, would be useful to the students of this interesting and too much neglected branch of microscopic '''phytotomy'''.|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=guIUAAAAYAAJ&dq=%22phytotomy%22&pg=PA143#v=onepage&q=%22phytotomy%22&f=false|author=George Gulliver|title=List of Plants which afford Raphides, Sphæraphides, Long Crystal Prisms, and Short Prismatic Crystals}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Essentials of Anatomy|author=William Darling|year=1895|passage=Anatomy may be divided into two great classes, '''''Phytotomy''''', or vegetable anatomy, and ''Zoötomy'', or animal anatomy.|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=bUAUNVHXjaEC&dq=%22phytotomy%22&pg=PA1#v=onepage&q=%22phytotomy%22&f=false}}

